From e69e44e522beada9d5d56cfa85c3116e596473c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] tests: run the suite on Qt 4.8

QSignalSpy and connect() sites use the SIGNAL()/SLOT() string form, lambda
slots became member slots, qOverload<> disambiguations became explicit
signatures, and Qt5-only calls (QByteArrayLiteral, toSecsSinceEpoch, cbegin,
QUrl::FullyDecoded, QSignalSpy::wait, QWidget::grab, the static
QFileInfo::exists(), QStringList::join(QChar), toHtmlEscaped, emitting
another object's signal) got all-version forms or guarded fallbacks. The
locale test gains the same Qt4 lrelease recipe and locale.qrc as src/.
Nothing is excluded: all 27 test binaries pass on Qt 4.8.7 (Xvfb) and the
sources still build unchanged on Qt 5.15/6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SNLMjDKKUDw5GKpBW96KSN
